warning[SCXML061]: `retry-count` is not an ECMAScript identifier: it contains `-`
  --> tests/ui/scxml061-ecmascript-data-id.scxml:3:15
   |
 3 |     <data id="retry-count" expr="0"/>
   |               ^^^^^^^^^^^ `-` cannot appear in an identifier
...
 9 |     <transition event="fail" cond="retry-count &lt; 3" target="a">
   |                                    ----------- `retry-count` is referenced here
   |
   = note: the ECMAScript data model creates this variable (SCXML 1.0 §B.2.1) as a property of the global object, reachable only as `globalThis['retry-count']`; `retry-count` in an expression is not this variable: `-` subtracts, so `retry-count` reads two variables
   = help: to use the variable in expressions, name it with an identifier that is also an XML ID, such as `retryCount`, and rename every reference to it
   = spec: SCXML 1.0 §5.3 <data>
   = spec: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model
help: rename the variable to `retryCount` here and in 4 references
   |
 3 |     <data id="retryCount" expr="0"/>
   |               ~~~~~~~~~~
...
 9 |     <transition event="fail" cond="retryCount &lt; 3" target="a">
   |                                    ~~~~~~~~~~
10 |       <assign location="retryCount" expr="retryCount + 1"/>
   |                         ~~~~~~~~~~        ~~~~~~~~~~
11 |       <log label="retry" expr="'attempt ' + retryCount"/>
   |                                             ~~~~~~~~~~

